From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Oct 2026 05:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_pm8150b_charger: honour the USB-C/PD input budget

On a USB-C source (dock, PD charger) the PM8150B's BC1.2 detection (APSD)
never completes, so the driver stayed at the hardware's USB 2.0 default of
500 mA for the whole session, re-ran APSD every second and logged "Apsd not
ready" three times a second. A docked Retroid Pocket 5 at Steam's home
screen drew 500 mA from a 5 V / 2 A PD contract and charged its battery only
at a trickle (measured 2026-10-11, blackbox + regmap); the same device running
all night at that cap ran its battery flat (PMIC UVLO, 2026-10-12).

- USBIN_CURRENT_LIMIT_CFG only counts in software-override mode: set
  ICL_OVERRIDE for any limit above the SDP default, clear it for 500 mA so
  the hardware keeps handling plain SDP ports.
- Take the input budget from the Type-C port manager's source supply
  (tcpm-source-psy-*: the PD contract current, or the Rp it saw on CC) via a
  power-supply notifier, falling back to the PMIC's own TYPE_C_SNK_STATUS Rp
  bits; BC1.2 results only decide for legacy sources.
- Re-run APSD at most five times per plug, then settle for 500 mA quietly.
- Reset to 500 mA on unplug; report "online" as a boolean (upowerd logged
  'value "TRUE" of type gboolean is invalid' three times a second on 16).
- Log the limit once per change at info level.

- v2 (linux-pocknix-sm8250 17): look the port manager's supply up on every
  evaluation instead of caching an unreferenced pointer to another device.
- v3 (linux-pocknix-sm8250 19): the mode bits were wrong. CMD_ICL_OVERRIDE's
  ICL_OVERRIDE is the USB 2.0/3.0 (100/500/900 mA) override: v1/v2 set it
  with a 2 A limit and the chip applied exactly 500 mA (ICL_STATUS 0x0a on
  the docked 2026-10-11 boot) while the log said 2000 mA; the full battery
  discharged on the dock and the device died overnight on a powered hub. Now
  as the vendor driver's smblib_icl_override(): high-current mode =
  USBIN_MODE_CHG set, ICL_OVERRIDE clear, ICL_OVERRIDE_AFTER_APSD set, and
  BC1.2 detection (APSD) off for the duration of a PD contract; the 500 mA
  fallback is the chip's own auto mode. The log names where each figure came
  from (USB PD contract / Type-C advertisement / Type-C Rp / BC1.2 / none).

Holodor patch 0722 (linux-pocknix-sm8250 16, v2 in 17, v3 in 19).

v4 (2026-10-12): a PD contract is always applied in software mode, whatever
its size. v3 put contracts of 500 mA and below into hardware auto mode with
APSD off, and the chip then used its stale APSD result: on a hub offering
5 V / 0.5 A the Retroid Pocket 5 sat at ICL_MAX 3 A and drew 2 A.

v5 (2026-10-12): accept PD voltages above 5 V. The chip's discrete adapter
allowance (USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_CFG 5 V / 9-12 V windows) flagged USBIN_OV when
a source stepped 5 V -> 9 V, suspended the input and left the battery
discharging while docked (Retroid Pocket 5, kernel 21 with a 9 V sink PDO).
Vendor recipe: USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_OVERRIDE = CONTINUOUS and the continuous
AICL threshold = contract voltage - 1 V (floor 4.0 V). The switcher frequency
is left alone (the chip already runs the vendor's 9 V setting, 0x150 = 0x08).
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pm8150b_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pm8150b_charger.c
@@ -129,6 +129,20 @@
 #define USBIN_PLUGIN_RT_STS_BIT			BIT(4)
 
 #define USBIN_CMD_IL				0x340
+/*
+ * Input voltage allowance override (vendor smblib_usb_pd_adapter_allowance_
+ * override): FORCE_x pins the accepted VBUS level, CONTINUOUS accepts any
+ * level up to the chip's absolute limit. Without it the chip sits on
+ * USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_CFG's discrete 5 V / 9-12 V windows and flags USBIN_OV
+ * on a PD source stepping from 5 V to 9 V (Retroid Pocket 5, 2026-10-12: input
+ * suspended, battery discharging while docked).
+ */
+#define USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_OVERRIDE		0x344
+#define USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_OVERRIDE_MASK	GENMASK(3, 0)
+#define USBIN_ADAPTER_FORCE_5V_BIT		BIT(0)
+#define USBIN_ADAPTER_FORCE_9V_BIT		BIT(1)
+#define USBIN_ADAPTER_FORCE_12V_BIT		BIT(2)
+#define USBIN_ADAPTER_CONTINUOUS_BIT		BIT(3)
 #define USBIN_SUSPEND_BIT			BIT(0)
 
 #define CMD_APSD				0x341
@@ -286,6 +300,11 @@
  * @batt_info:		Battery data from DT
  * @status_change_work: Worker to handle plug/unplug events
  * @cable_irq:		USB plugin IRQ
+ * @psy_nb:		power-supply notifier: follows the Type-C port manager's source supply
+ * @icl_ua:		input current limit last written (0 = not yet)
+ * @apsd_reruns:	APSD re-runs on the current plug
+ * @icl_src:		where the limit's figure came from (logged once per change)
+ * @icl_pd:		a USB PD contract set the limit (BC1.2 detection off meanwhile)
  * @wakeup_enabled:	If the cable IRQ will cause a wakeup
  * @usb_in_i_chan:	USB_IN current measurement channel
  * @usb_in_v_chan:	USB_IN voltage measurement channel
@@ -302,6 +321,14 @@
 	int cable_irq;
 	bool wakeup_enabled;
 
+	/* Type-C: follow the port manager's source supply (PD contract / Rp) */
+	struct notifier_block psy_nb;
+	unsigned int icl_ua;
+	int apsd_reruns;
+	unsigned int input_uv;
+	const char *icl_src;
+	bool icl_pd;
+
 	struct iio_channel *usb_in_i_chan;
 	struct iio_channel *usb_in_v_chan;
 
@@ -331,7 +358,7 @@
 		return rc;
 	}
 
-	*val = (stat & USBIN_PLUGIN_RT_STS_BIT);
+	*val = !!(stat & USBIN_PLUGIN_RT_STS_BIT);
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -357,7 +384,7 @@
 		return rc;
 	}
 	if (!(apsd_stat & APSD_DTC_STATUS_DONE_BIT)) {
-		dev_err(chip->dev, "Apsd not ready");
+		dev_dbg(chip->dev, "Apsd not ready");
 		return -EAGAIN;
 	}
 
@@ -446,9 +473,59 @@
 	return rc;
 }
 
-static int smb5_set_current_limit(struct smb5_chip *chip, unsigned int val)
+/*
+ * Input current limit modes, as the vendor driver's smblib_icl_override()
+ * uses them on this PMIC:
+ *  - high current: the limit is USBIN_CURRENT_LIMIT_CFG. USBIN_MODE_CHG set
+ *    (the init sequence does that), CMD_ICL_OVERRIDE clear and
+ *    ICL_OVERRIDE_AFTER_APSD set, so a BC1.2 result never replaces the limit.
+ *    The vendor driver also switches BC1.2 detection (APSD) off for the
+ *    duration of a PD contract, which never completes APSD anyway; so do we.
+ *  - hardware auto: USBIN_MODE_CHG set, both override bits clear, APSD on:
+ *    the chip applies what APSD derives, 500 mA until BC1.2 says otherwise.
+ *    The chip's power-on behaviour and our fallback without a Type-C budget.
+ *    Never used with APSD off: the chip then applies a stale result.
+ * CMD_ICL_OVERRIDE's ICL_OVERRIDE bit is the USB 2.0/3.0 (100/500/900 mA)
+ * override, not a high-current one: with it set and 2 A written to the limit
+ * register the chip applied exactly 500 mA (ICL_STATUS = AICL_STATUS = 0x0a
+ * on a docked Retroid Pocket 5, 2026-10-11) and a running device drained its
+ * battery overnight on a 5 V / 2 A contract while the log said 2000 mA. v1/v2
+ * of this patch did exactly that.
+ */
+static int smb5_set_icl_mode(struct smb5_chip *chip, bool high_current,
+			     bool apsd)
+{
+	int rc;
+
+	rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + USBIN_ICL_OPTIONS,
+				USBIN_MODE_CHG_BIT, USBIN_MODE_CHG_BIT);
+	if (rc < 0)
+		return rc;
+	rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + CMD_ICL_OVERRIDE,
+				ICL_OVERRIDE_BIT, 0);
+	if (rc < 0)
+		return rc;
+	rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + USBIN_LOAD_CFG,
+				ICL_OVERRIDE_AFTER_APSD_BIT,
+				high_current ? ICL_OVERRIDE_AFTER_APSD_BIT : 0);
+	if (rc < 0)
+		return rc;
+	return regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap,
+				  chip->base + USBIN_OPTIONS_1_CFG,
+				  BC1P2_SRC_DETECT_BIT,
+				  apsd ? BC1P2_SRC_DETECT_BIT : 0);
+}
+
+/*
+ * @val: the input current limit; @pd: a USB PD contract set it (BC1.2
+ * detection is switched off for its duration); @src: where the figure came
+ * from, logged once per change.
+ */
+static int smb5_set_current_limit(struct smb5_chip *chip, unsigned int val,
+				  bool pd, const char *src)
 {
 	unsigned char val_raw;
+	int rc;
 
 	if (val > 4950000) {
 		dev_err(chip->dev,
@@ -457,13 +534,163 @@
 	}
 	val_raw = val / CURRENT_SCALE_FACTOR;
 
-	return regmap_write(chip->regmap, chip->base + USBIN_CURRENT_LIMIT_CFG,
-		val_raw);
+	rc = regmap_write(chip->regmap, chip->base + USBIN_CURRENT_LIMIT_CFG,
+			  val_raw);
+	if (rc < 0)
+		return rc;
+
+	/*
+	 * A PD contract is always applied in software, whatever its size: with
+	 * BC1.2 detection switched off, hardware auto mode has no fresh result
+	 * to work from and falls back to whatever APSD_RESULT_STATUS last held
+	 * (2026-10-12: a hub offering 5 V / 0.5 A, the chip at 3 A on a stale
+	 * QC 2.0 result, 2 A actually drawn against the 0.5 A contract).
+	 */
+	rc = smb5_set_icl_mode(chip, pd || val > SDP_CURRENT_UA, !pd);
+	if (rc < 0)
+		return rc;
+
+	if (chip->icl_ua != val || chip->icl_src != src)
+		dev_info(chip->dev, "input current limit %u mA (%s)\n",
+			 val / 1000, src);
+	chip->icl_ua = val;
+	chip->icl_pd = pd;
+	chip->icl_src = src;
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* The Rp a Type-C source advertises on CC, as our sink limit (0 = default/none) */
+static unsigned int smb5_typec_rp_current(struct smb5_chip *chip)
+{
+	unsigned int stat;
+
+	if (regmap_read(chip->regmap, chip->base + TYPE_C_SNK_STATUS, &stat) < 0)
+		return 0;
+	if (stat & SNK_RP_3P0_BIT)
+		return 3000000;
+	if (stat & SNK_RP_1P5_BIT)
+		return 1500000;
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Accept the contract voltage on USBIN. The vendor driver sets the allowance
+ * before its own PD stack requests a level; the Type-C port manager tells us
+ * only after the source has switched, so the allowance is CONTINUOUS from
+ * init on and only the continuous-mode AICL threshold follows the contract
+ * (vendor: contract minus 1 V, floor 4.0 V; 0x384 encodes 4.0-5.5 V in
+ * 100 mV steps, 5.6 V and up in 200 mV steps from raw 16).
+ */
+static int smb5_set_input_voltage(struct smb5_chip *chip, unsigned int uv)
+{
+	unsigned int mv, thr_mv, raw;
+	int rc;
+
+	if (!uv)
+		uv = 5000000;
+	mv = uv / 1000;
+	thr_mv = mv > 5000 ? mv - 1000 : 4000;
+	if (thr_mv < 5600)
+		raw = (thr_mv - 4000) / 100;
+	else
+		raw = (thr_mv - 5600) / 200 + 16;
+	raw = min_t(unsigned int, raw, USBIN_CONT_AICL_THRESHOLD_CFG_MASK);
+
+	rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap,
+				chip->base + USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_OVERRIDE,
+				USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_OVERRIDE_MASK,
+				USBIN_ADAPTER_CONTINUOUS_BIT);
+	if (rc < 0)
+		return rc;
+	rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap,
+				chip->base + USBIN_CONT_AICL_THRESHOLD_CFG,
+				USBIN_CONT_AICL_THRESHOLD_CFG_MASK, raw);
+	if (rc < 0)
+		return rc;
+	if (chip->input_uv != uv)
+		dev_info(chip->dev,
+			 "input voltage %u mV: continuous allowance, AICL threshold %u mV\n",
+			 mv, thr_mv);
+	chip->input_uv = uv;
+	return 0;
+}
+
+struct smb5_typec_budget {
+	unsigned int current_ua;
+	unsigned int voltage_uv;
+	bool pd;
+};
+
+static int smb5_typec_budget_cb(struct power_supply *psy, void *data)
+{
+	struct smb5_typec_budget *budget = data;
+	union power_supply_propval val;
+
+	if (strncmp(psy->desc->name, "tcpm-source-psy-", 16))
+		return 0;
+	if (power_supply_get_property(psy, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE, &val) < 0 ||
+	    !val.intval)
+		return 1;
+	if (power_supply_get_property(psy, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_MAX,
+				      &val) < 0)
+		return 1;
+	if (val.intval > 0)
+		budget->current_ua = val.intval;
+	if (!power_supply_get_property(psy, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW, &val) &&
+	    val.intval > 0)
+		budget->voltage_uv = val.intval;
+	if (!power_supply_get_property(psy, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_USB_TYPE, &val))
+		budget->pd = val.intval == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_PD ||
+			     val.intval == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_PD_DRP ||
+			     val.intval == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_PD_PPS ||
+			     val.intval == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_PD_SPR_AVS ||
+			     val.intval == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_PD_PPS_SPR_AVS;
+	return 1;
+}
+
+/*
+ * What the Type-C port manager negotiated: the USB PD contract current (pd
+ * set), or the Rp current it saw on CC. The port manager's supply is looked
+ * up on every evaluation (it is another device that may come and go; no
+ * pointer to it is kept). current_ua 0 = nothing attached, default Rp, or no
+ * port manager.
+ */
+static void smb5_typec_psy_budget(struct smb5_typec_budget *budget)
+{
+	memset(budget, 0, sizeof(*budget));
+	power_supply_for_each_psy(budget, smb5_typec_budget_cb);
+}
+
+static int smb5_psy_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long event,
+			     void *data)
+{
+	struct smb5_chip *chip = container_of(nb, struct smb5_chip, psy_nb);
+	struct power_supply *psy = data;
+
+	if (event != PSY_EVENT_PROP_CHANGED || psy == chip->chg_psy)
+		return NOTIFY_OK;
+	if (strncmp(psy->desc->name, "tcpm-source-psy-", 16))
+		return NOTIFY_OK;
+
+	/* the PD contract lands a moment after the plug: re-evaluate the limit */
+	mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &chip->status_change_work,
+			 msecs_to_jiffies(200));
+	return NOTIFY_OK;
+}
+
+static void smb5_unreg_psy_notifier(void *data)
+{
+	struct smb5_chip *chip = data;
+
+	power_supply_unreg_notifier(&chip->psy_nb);
 }
 
 static void smb5_status_change_work(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	unsigned int charger_type, current_ua;
+	struct smb5_typec_budget budget;
+	const char *src;
+	bool pd = false;
 	int usb_online = 0;
 	int count, rc;
 	struct smb5_chip *chip;
@@ -471,8 +698,32 @@
 	chip = container_of(work, struct smb5_chip, status_change_work.work);
 
 	smb5_get_prop_usb_online(chip, &usb_online);
-	if (!usb_online)
+	if (!usb_online) {
+		/* back to the hardware's 500 mA default for whatever comes next */
+		chip->apsd_reruns = 0;
+		smb5_set_input_voltage(chip, 5000000);
+		smb5_set_current_limit(chip, SDP_CURRENT_UA, false, "unplugged");
 		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * A USB-C source states its budget without BC1.2: the PD contract (via
+	 * the Type-C port manager's supply) or the Rp it advertises on CC, and
+	 * that figure is binding. BC1.2 (APSD) only decides for legacy sources,
+	 * and on a PD source APSD often never completes at all.
+	 */
+	smb5_typec_psy_budget(&budget);
+	if (budget.current_ua) {
+		current_ua = budget.current_ua;
+		pd = budget.pd;
+		src = pd ? "USB PD contract" : "Type-C current advertisement";
+		goto apply;
+	}
+	current_ua = smb5_typec_rp_current(chip);
+	if (current_ua) {
+		src = "Type-C Rp";
+		goto apply;
+	}
 
 	for (count = 0; count < 3; count++) {
 		dev_dbg(chip->dev, "get charger type retry %d\n", count);
@@ -488,14 +739,27 @@
 	}
 
 	if (rc < 0) {
-		rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + CMD_APSD,
-					APSD_RERUN_BIT, APSD_RERUN_BIT);
-		schedule_delayed_work(&chip->status_change_work,
-				      msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
-		dev_dbg(chip->dev, "get charger type failed, rerun apsd\n");
-		return;
+		/*
+		 * Re-run APSD a few times, then settle for the 500 mA default
+		 * instead of retrying (and logging) every second for the whole
+		 * session.
+		 */
+		if (chip->apsd_reruns++ < 5) {
+			regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + CMD_APSD,
+					   APSD_RERUN_BIT, APSD_RERUN_BIT);
+			schedule_delayed_work(&chip->status_change_work,
+					      msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
+			dev_dbg(chip->dev, "charger type not ready, rerun apsd\n");
+			return;
+		}
+		dev_dbg(chip->dev, "charger type never detected, keeping %u mA\n",
+			SDP_CURRENT_UA / 1000);
+		current_ua = SDP_CURRENT_UA;
+		src = "no BC1.2 result";
+		goto apply;
 	}
 
+	src = "BC1.2";
 	switch (charger_type) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_CDP:
 		current_ua = CDP_CURRENT_UA;
@@ -509,7 +773,10 @@
 		break;
 	}
 
-	smb5_set_current_limit(chip, current_ua);
+apply:
+	current_ua = min_t(unsigned int, current_ua, CURRENT_MAX_UA);
+	smb5_set_input_voltage(chip, pd ? budget.voltage_uv : 5000000);
+	smb5_set_current_limit(chip, current_ua, pd, src);
 	power_supply_changed(chip->chg_psy);
 }
 
@@ -614,7 +881,8 @@
 
 	switch (psp) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_MAX:
-		return smb5_set_current_limit(chip, val->intval);
+		return smb5_set_current_limit(chip, val->intval, false,
+					      "userspace");
 	default:
 		dev_err(chip->dev, "No setter for property: %d\n", psp);
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -790,6 +1058,12 @@
 					     "%s: init command %d failed\n",
 					     __func__, i);
 	}
+
+	/* any PD level is welcome from the start; threshold for 5 V until known */
+	rc = smb5_set_input_voltage(chip, 5000000);
+	if (rc < 0)
+		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc,
+				     "%s: input allowance failed\n", __func__);
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -884,6 +1158,15 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc,
 				     "Failed to init status change work\n");
 
+	chip->psy_nb.notifier_call = smb5_psy_notifier;
+	rc = power_supply_reg_notifier(&chip->psy_nb);
+	if (rc)
+		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc,
+				     "Failed to register power supply notifier\n");
+	rc = devm_add_action_or_reset(chip->dev, smb5_unreg_psy_notifier, chip);
+	if (rc)
+		return rc;
+
 	rc = (chip->batt_info->voltage_max_design_uv - 3487500) / 7500 + 1;
 	rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + FLOAT_VOLTAGE_CFG,
 				FLOAT_VOLTAGE_SETTING_MASK, rc);
